**[Wick Gives Up What He Knows — Glasstaff]**

**GM** — *as Wick, on Glasstaff's capabilities*
> "Glasstaff? He's a wizard, not just a muscle with a title. I've seen him drop a man with a spell, no weapon drawn, nobody messes with him twice."

**GM** — *as Wick, on the dungeon's lower levels; note: Wick slips from third to first person mid-sentence ("Wick's only ever been sent to the… I've only been sent to")*
> "And he goes, there's more than what… you know, this has got… this dungeon's got multiple levels, you already know this. Wick's only ever been sent to the… I've only been sent to the subterranean part once to carry supplies, and I don't want to go back. Don't know what's there, but it's kinda wrong. There's something really wrong over there that messes with your head, I'm told."

**GM** — *as Wick, on Glasstaff's unknown superior; GM trails off before finishing Glasstaff's name*
> "Then he… So then you asked about who does he report to, right? He goes, yeah, Glasstaff answers to somebody. I've overheard him complaining about orders from town, and once about the boss's business… But, I mean, I think it's somebody in Phandalin, but I don't think, I don't think Glasstaff"

---

**[The Black Spider — Wick Flinches]**

**Zenvon** — *pressing on the name*
> "Black Spider."

**GM** — *narrating Wick's physical reaction*
> "He kind of flinches when you say it. But… Kind of as if he could feel some… you could see how uncomfortable that name makes him. But he doesn't know anything about it. Do you want to press him on the topic?"

**Zenvon** — *deciding to press*
> "Yes, I want to question on the topic. So we'll… Insight, or investigation, what do I do?"

**GM** — *directing the roll*
> "Yeah, roll the insight. I mean, no, just roll intimidation."

**Zenvon** — *rolling, mishearing or mis-saying the skill name*
> "Integration."

**GM** — *as Wick, after the roll; Wick retreats*
> "Alright, he goes, look dude, I just carry crates, alright? You start asking about the boss's boss, that's how people end up carrying less."

---

**[The Insight Roll — Wick's Yes Is a Lie]**

**GM** — *calling for a roll to read Wick's sincerity*
> "He's a role, role in investigation or insight. With advantage."

**GM** — *after the roll resolves*
> "That said, okay. He says yes."

**Zenvon** — *pressing for more before fully committing*
> "In order to trust you, you're gonna tell me all the secrets about this manor? Like, what's upstairs?"

**GM** — *delivering the insight result; Wick's "yes" exposed as a lie of convenience*
> "Wait, hold on, hold on, Hilton He goes, he goes, you, okay, he says yes, but you know he's lying. What you really, the impression you get is he's gonna take whatever money you have and get out of, get out of Dodge as fast as possible."

**Zenvon** — *reacting to the revelation*
> "Are you taking our money? Okay."

**GM** — *clarifying the precise nature of Wick's intent*
> "Well, you're offering it to him, he is, he is a cr."
> "Right, I'm just telling you, so"
> "So he takes your money and says, of course I'm with you, boss. And then at his first opportunity, he's going to run away."
> "But you definitely do not get the impression that he's gonna try to backstab you. He's basically looking at the money as a way to get out of here."

**GM** — *OOC, giving Zenvon the option to decide*
> "So what do you want to do with him? Do you want to let him… do you want… do you give him the money and let him follow you, or are you. Or let him run away. He's just one lowly thug."

---

**[The Dendrar Revelation — Under Pressure]**

**Zenvon** — *choosing to press further rather than release Wick*
> "This is such a tough choice. Hold on. I wanna, you know, try to get more information from him, so… I wanna tie him up and, you know. Shove his face into the system and get more information from you."

**GM** — *as Wick, cracking under duress; names the Dendrar family*
> "The only additional piece of information, he's kind of, like, really upset over this at this point in time. He's, like, shitting his pants, and he says that there was this family, the Dendrars, that the Redbrands handled a while back."

**GM** — *OOC, connecting the dots for the player*
> "Yes, that's the family you guys rescued. Right, okay, that makes sense, okay."

---

**[Zenvon Executes Wick — No Roll Required]**

**Zenvon** — *making the decision*
> "Yeah, I mean, I would prefer to attack him at this point instead of letting him run away."

**GM** — *waiving the combat roll for a helpless prisoner*
> "Alright, so you're going to attack him. Alright, roll for… alright, you kill him. He's a poor, defenseless guy. He's dead. We don't have, we don't have to roll for, combat."

---

**[Cistern Search — The Hidden Satchel]**

**Zenvon** — *noting the unexplored area*
> "Did we get anything here? There are so many crates and barrels."

**GM** — *describing the find*
> "Alright, so, it turns out that the barrels have, like, food and things like that, right? But you do notice a waterproof satchel which hangs from a submerged rope attached to the south wall of the cistern about 2 feet below the water's surface."
> "You find inside of it a satchel hidden… you find a satchel which contains a potion of healing and a potion of invisibility."

